The user wants "the verified claims as JSON". The user's goals (from compaction summary) don't explicitly require no_secret_leakage/no_credential_leakage as Proof properties — the goal list says "Must return verified claims as JSON" and "Never use a fallback secret". The property goals in pi_goal_check include no_secret_leakage and no_credential_leakage as available goals, but the user didn't demand them.

Hmm, but returning claims is inherently "JWT payload returned to client" — the no_credential_leakage property would flag ANY handler that returns claims. So the narrow Proof must exclude it. That's the compiler-sanctioned route per the ZTS500 suggestion itself.

